{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"6f78901234567890","type":"group","x":1000,"y":-100,"width":750,"height":850,"color":"5","label":"Progressive Disclosure Architecture"},
		{"id":"3c4d5e6f78901234","type":"group","x":-900,"y":-100,"width":700,"height":600,"color":"1","label":"Evolution"},
		{"id":"0123456789012345","type":"group","x":-900,"y":600,"width":700,"height":500,"color":"3","label":"Implementation"},
		{"id":"2345678901234567","type":"group","x":-100,"y":600,"width":1000,"height":500,"color":"4","label":"Core Capabilities"},
		{"id":"5678901234567890","type":"group","x":1000,"y":850,"width":750,"height":520,"color":"1","label":"Security & Best Practices"},
		{"id":"1a2b3c4d5e6f7890","type":"text","text":"# 🚀 Future Outlook: 2026 - The Year of Agent Skills\n\n- **Industry Adoption**: Major LLM providers adopting Agent Skills as standard for \"AI Apps\"\n- **Self-Evolution**: Agents will create, edit, and evaluate their own skills\n- **Portability**: Cross-platform standardization (similar to MCP adoption curve)\n- **Ecosystem**: Shift from custom-built agents to standardized, shareable capabilities","x":0,"y":-600,"width":800,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"2b3c4d5e6f789012","type":"text","text":"# 🎯 Agent Skills - Core Concept\n\n## The Formula\n**Agent = General LLM + Collection of Specific Skills**\n\n**Definition**: Standardized, composable directories of instructions, scripts, and resources that equip general-purpose AI models with specialized domain expertise without fragmenting the model itself.\n\n**Interface**: Simple files and folders - just like employee onboarding guides","x":-100,"y":0,"width":1000,"height":250,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"3456789012345678","type":"text","text":"# ⚡ Key Capabilities\n\n## 1. Deterministic Code Execution\n- Run Python/Bash scripts for reliable outputs\n- **Avoid hallucination** on math/sorting tasks\n- More efficient than token generation\n- *Example*: PDF field extraction via script vs LLM parsing\n\n## 2. Portability & Scalability\n- **Unbinds context window limits**\n- Load only what's needed, when needed\n- Cross-platform, easily shared\n- Version controlled like code\n\n## 3. Composability\n- Mix and match skills dynamically\n- One agent → many expertise domains\n- Reusable across projects/teams","x":-50,"y":650,"width":450,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4567890123456789","type":"text","text":"# 💼 Real-World Use Cases\n\n## Corporate Procedures\n- Onboarding guides\n- Project update protocols\n- Code review standards\n\n## Domain Expertise\n- PDF manipulation\n- Data analysis workflows\n- API integration patterns\n\n## Developer Workflows\n- Testing procedures\n- Deployment checklists\n- Documentation generation","x":450,"y":650,"width":420,"height":810,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7890123456789012","type":"text","text":"# 📋 Level 1: Metadata (Always Loaded)\n\n**What**: YAML header with name + description\n**When**: At agent startup, injected into system prompt\n**Size**: Minimal (few lines)\n**Purpose**: Let agent know skill exists without consuming context\n\n```yaml\nname: PDF Processing\ndescription: Extract and manipulate PDF forms\n```","x":1050,"y":-50,"width":650,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8901234567890123","type":"text","text":"# 📖 Level 2: Instructional Context (On Decision)\n\n**What**: Full `skill.md` body content\n**When**: Agent determines skill is relevant to user request\n**Size**: Medium (procedures, guidelines, examples)\n**Purpose**: Understand HOW to use the skill\n\n*Example*: When user says \"fill out this PDF\", agent reads PDF processing instructions","x":1050,"y":200,"width":650,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9012345678901234","type":"text","text":"# 🔧 Level 3: Deep Resources (On Demand)\n\n**What**: External files, scripts, templates, data\n**When**: Specific sub-task explicitly requires them\n**Size**: Large (Python scripts, reference docs, datasets)\n**Purpose**: Execute deterministic operations and access detailed knowledge\n\n*Example*: `extract_fields.py` script only runs when extracting PDF form data","x":1050,"y":470,"width":650,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6789012345678901","type":"text","text":"# ⚠️ Security Risks\n\n- **Code Execution**: Skills can run shell commands and scripts\n- **File System Access**: Potential for data exfiltration\n- **Network Connections**: External API calls and data transmission\n- **Dependency Vulnerabilities**: Third-party library risks\n\n**Critical**: Treat skills like software dependencies - audit before use!","x":1050,"y":900,"width":650,"height":210,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"7890123456789013","type":"text","text":"# ✅ Best Practices\n\n1. **Audit all skills** before installation\n2. **Review code dependencies** and external imports\n3. **Check network instructions** for data transmission\n4. **Use trusted sources** for skill libraries\n5. **Version control** skills like code\n6. **Test in isolation** before production use","x":1050,"y":1150,"width":650,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8901234567890124","type":"text","text":"# 🔄 Development Workflow\n\n1. **Identify Gaps**: Observe where agents struggle\n2. **Reflective Codification**: Capture successful approaches in Markdown\n3. **Split Context**: Keep files focused and modular (separate concerns)\n4. **Security Audit**: Review before deployment\n5. **Iterate**: Continuously improve based on usage patterns","x":-100,"y":300,"width":1000,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"4d5e6f7890123456","type":"text","text":"# 📊 2025 Approach (Old Way)\n\n### Monolithic Agents\n- Built distinct, single-purpose agents\n- **Marketing Agent**, **Sales Agent**, **Support Agent**\n- Hard-coded resources and capabilities\n- Rigid, non-portable solutions\n- Fragmented model architecture\n\n**Problem**: Every use case requires a new agent build","x":-850,"y":-50,"width":600,"height":250,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5e6f789012345678","type":"text","text":"# ✨ 2026 Approach (Agent Skills)\n\n### Composable Skill Libraries\n- Modular skills: **Figma Skill**, **PDF Analysis Skill**\n- Dynamic attachment to general LLMs\n- Portable, shareable, version-controlled\n- Plug-and-play expertise\n\n**Solution**: One LLM + skill library = infinite specialized agents","x":-850,"y":250,"width":600,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1234567890123456","type":"text","text":"# 📁 File Structure Example\n\n```\n/pdf-processing-skill/\n├── skill.md              # Core instructions + YAML\n├── forms.md              # Sub-instructions\n├── reference.md          # Documentation\n└── scripts/\n    ├── extract_fields.py # Deterministic execution\n    └── fill_form.py      # PDF manipulation\n```\n\n**Key Principle**: Files and folders as interface\n- Simple to create, share, version control\n- Easy to audit for security\n- Familiar developer workflow","x":-850,"y":650,"width":600,"height":420,"color":"3"}
	],
